--!strict
--==============================================================================
-- TANGLEMIRE, AS APPROVED
--
-- The five plants, the shared Mire-Cage Pod and Miremaw were designed as
-- temporary Edit-mode models under `Workspace.TanglemireApprovalPreview` and
-- `Workspace.TanglemirePodApprovalPreview`, reviewed there, and approved there.
-- This file is those models, lifted part for part on 2026-08-27 and frozen.
--
-- IT IS DATA, NOT ART DIRECTION. Nothing here was redrawn, retimed, recoloured
-- or tidied on the way across; every size, CFrame, colour and material is the
-- number that was approved. A preview folder is a scratchpad that gets deleted,
-- so the approved geometry had to stop living in one -- but "translate it into
-- code" only counts if the translation is lossless, and the proof that it is
-- lossless is recorded in KB/HANDOFF.
--
-- CFRAMES CARRY ALL TWELVE COMPONENTS. Euler angles would read better and would
-- not round-trip exactly. Sixty-seven of Miremaw's seventy-three parts are
-- rotated off-axis; "reads better" is not worth moving approved art.
--
-- WHAT SCALES, AND HOW
--
--   plants   authored at a fixed preview height and replayed through ONE
--            factor, hs = FrameHeight(sp, kg) / PreviewHeight[id]. That is the
--            trick Suncrown already uses: a preview drawn on its own curve is
--            conformed to the shared frame by a single multiplier, so nothing
--            downstream has to know the mockup used different maths. Each
--            species Height in SeedData IS its PreviewHeight, so hs is exactly
--            1.0 at the median weight and the live plant is the mockup.
--
--   pod      stored as FRACTIONS OF DIAMETER, so it is exact at every weight
--            rather than only at the three that were approved. Fourteen of its
--            sixteen parts agreed across the three approved diameters to
--            5.7e-5 -- float noise -- which is what makes that legal.
--
--   Miremaw  studs at preview scale. MiremawModel owns its rig and its own
--            scale factor, the same contract BramblebackModel already has.
--
-- Colours are absolute EXCEPT the pod's Shell, Crown and FloodSeam, which are
-- painted at runtime from SeedData.ColorForKg -- the shell says what the pod is
-- worth, and that must never become a species tell.
--==============================================================================

export type PartSpec = {
	name: string,
	shape: string,
	size: Vector3,
	cf: CFrame,
	color: Color3?,
	material: Enum.Material,
	transparency: number?,
	reflectance: number?,
}

